    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0365" n="199" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg199"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.77/1633</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-10T10:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 10, 1917, 10 a.m</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My telegram August 9, 10 a.m. Please inform whether the British Government has
                    expressed itself further concerning the protest which is now delaying the
                    construction of the American railway in Hunan, Hupeh, the survey having been
                    completed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
